{
  "title": "Namaz of Imam Zayn al-Abidin (a.s.)",
  "data": "Upon concluding the prayer, say the following supplication:\nيَا مَنْ اَظْهَرَ الْجَمِيْلَ\nYAA MAN AZHARAL JAMEELA\nO He Who has shown only goodness\nوَسَتَرَ الْقَبِيْحَ\nWA SATARAL QABEEHA\nand concealed the evil (deeds of His servants)!\nيَا مَنْ لَمْ يُؤَاخِذْ بِالْجَرِيْرَةِ\nYAA MAN LAM YO-AAKHIZ BIL JAREERATE\nO He Who has not censured for the offenses\nوَلَمْ يَهْتِكِ السِّتْرَ\nWA LAM YAHTEKIS SITRA\nand has not exposed the hidden!\nيَا عَظِيْمَ الْعَفْوِ\nYAA A’ZEEMAL A’FWE\nO He Who is Ample in pardoning!\nيَا حَسَنَ التَّجَاوُزِ\nYAA HASANAT TAJAAWOZE\nO He Who is Excellent in overlooking!\nيَا وَاسِعَ الْمَغْفِرَةِ\nYAA WAASE-A’L MAGHFERATE\nO He Who is Liberal in forgiving!\nيَا بَاسِطَ الْيَدَيْنِ بِالرَّحْمَةِ\nYAA BAASETAL YADAYNE BIR RAHMATE\nO He Who opens His hands wide with mercy!\nيَا صَاحِبَ كُلِّ نَجْوٰى\nYAA SAAHEBA KULLE NAJWAA\nO He Who is present in all confidential talks!\nيَا مُنْتَهٰى كُلِّ شَكْوٰى\nYAA MUNTAHAA KULLE SHAKWAA\nO He Who is the ultimate objective of all complaints!\nيَا كَرِيْـمَ الصَّفْحِ\nYAA KAREEMAS SAFHE\nO He Who is Generous in condonation!\nيَا عَظِيْمَ الرَّجَاءِ\nYAA A’ZEEMAR RAJAAA-E\nO He Who is greatly hoped!\nيَا مُبْتَدِئاً بِالنِّعَمِ قَبْلَ اسْتِحْقَاقِهَا\nYAA MUBTADE-AN BIN NE-A’ME QABLAS TEHQAAQEHAA\nO He Who takes the initiative in favoring before they are deserved!\nيَا رَبَّنَا وَسَيِّدَنَا وَمَوْلَانَا\nYAA RABBANAA WA SAYYEDANAA WA MAWLAANAA\nO our Lord, our Master, and our Chief!\nيَا غَايَةَ رَغْبَتِنَا\nYAA GHAAYATA RAGHBATENAA\nO He Who is the ultimate of our desires!\nاَسْاَلُكَ اللّٰهُمَّ اَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nAS-ALOKAL LAAHUMMA AN TOSALLEYA A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALE MOHAMMADIN\nI beseech You, O Allah, to send blessings to Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad.",
  "merits": "In his book of Jamal al-Usbu', Sayyid Ibn Tawus has recorded a special prayer and supplication for each of the Holy Imams (a.s.), to be offered on Fridays.\nImam Zayn al-Abidin (a.s.)'s prayer consists of four units. In each unit, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) one hundred times."
}
